# Artificial Evolution's "target spell or permanent" (CR 115.1, 110.1): a player and a card in a hand are neither. With
# Bot2's Llanowar Elves spell on the stack, the same cast aimed at it is offered, which is the positive control that the
# refusals are for the target and not for a spell or a turn that could not be cast. (Trait Doctoring names a permanent only:
# trait-doctoring-targets-a-permanent-and-nothing-else.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Artificial Evolution
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Artificial Evolution.Cast(Bot2)
! Bot1.Hand.Artificial Evolution.Cast(Bot2.Hand.Forest)
Bot1.Hand.Artificial Evolution.Cast(Stack.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Elf)
Bot1.Modes(Goblin)

